# Architecture

## Stack (locked)

Django + DRF · **OSRM** routing · **Nominatim** geocoding · Open-Meteo · Vite + React + TypeScript · MapLibre (`react-map-gl`) + deck.gl. Frontend never calls OSRM, Nominatim, or Open-Meteo directly.

## Layering (do not blur)

| Layer | Owns | Must not |
|---|---|---|
| `planner/providers/*` | HTTP to OSRM / Nominatim / Open-Meteo, unit normalization, caching | Risk rules, ranking |
| `planner/domain/*` | Pure functions: checkpoints, ETAs, risk, ranking, heatmap grid | I/O, Django imports, HTTP |
| `planner/api/*` | Input validation, orchestration, response shape | Business rules inline |
| `frontend/src/api` | Typed fetch client | UI state |
| `frontend/src/map` | Layer builders, map view | Fetching, business rules |
| `frontend/src/components` | Form, cards, legend, slider | Risk math (backend owns it) |

## Endpoints

`GET /api/health` · `GET /api/locations` · `POST /api/plan` · `POST /api/heatmap`

## Data flow

`POST /api/plan` → geocode → OSRM up to 3 routes (via-point fallback if <3) → checkpoints + ETAs → batch Open-Meteo → classify → summarize → rank all → recommend #1 with warnings → response.
`POST /api/heatmap` (geometries + departure + load) → corridor grid (≤500 cells) → **49** hourly risk values per cell → response. Fetch after routes render.

## Invariants

1. Risk is computed **only** in `domain/risk.py`; the frontend renders levels, never recomputes them.
2. Provider responses are normalized to internal units (miles, mph, in/hr, UTC datetimes) at the provider boundary.
3. Independent provider calls (per route, per weather batch) run concurrently.
4. API keys live in backend env only. Never log or return them.
5. Response types are defined once per side (DRF serializers ↔ `frontend/src/types`) and kept in sync.
